  <sys:String x:Key="preset.gamer.name">Gamer Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.gamer.desc">One click for Game Mode, Game Bar/DVR off, a strong power plan, MMCSS, lighter visuals, less telemetry, SysMain off, and similar gaming tweaks. Read the preview list, then apply on a gaming PC.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.balanced.name">Balanced Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.balanced.desc">Light touch: Game Mode plus basic privacy, without aggressive service shutdowns. For when you want a bit of polish without risking Windows.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.minimal.name">Minimal / Server Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.minimal.desc">As lean as possible — telemetry, animations, background apps, unneeded services. Better for a second PC or HTPC; try Gamer first on your main gaming machine.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.laptop.name">Laptop / Battery Mode</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.laptop.desc">Skips aggressive gaming power tweaks and focuses on telemetry cuts, lighter visuals, and fewer background apps — balanced for battery life.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.privacymax.name">Maximum Privacy</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.privacymax.desc">More privacy than Balanced without going full Minimal: telemetry, location, advertising ID, and personalization tweaks in one profile.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.defaults.name">Restore Defaults (Undo Session)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="preset.defaults.desc">Reverts reversible changes from this WinCleaner session (Undo All). Removed apps don’t come back — reinstall those from the Store.</sys:String>
